@thiagoftsm `W: client_id provided is longer than 23 bytes, server might not allow that [MQTT-3.1.3-5]`

`[MQTT-3.1.3-5]` this is reference for MQTT specification and it states that server don't have to (but can) support client_id longer than 23 bytes. Most of servers do support long client_ids. But if server will not accept such connection it is not a bug. Therefore I print that as a warning.

We always used client_id of the same legth in past. Only difference is the new library give the user warning about it.
